-- mjVersionRange), bizapps-common 5.47.0 via `mj app install`, then this app's baseline
-- (V202607201423). `sync` blocks were stripped from a copy of metadata/ first so every record was
-- pushed. The push reported 0 errors: 25 created, 11 updated. A capture against core v6.1.4
-- produced the same procedure calls with the same parameter lists, in a different order.
--
-- WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. `mj app install` applies migrations and nothing else, and no
-- release before this one shipped a Metadata_Sync. Every host that installed v1.0.0 through
-- v2.0.0 without a manual `mj sync push` is missing the Secure Messages application, the
-- Secure Messaging action category, its 4 actions (Issue Portal Magic Link, Send Secure Message,
-- Start Secure Thread, Promote Thread) and their 19 params, and the entity overrides below.
--
-- UPDATES (11), checked column by column against a second database built from the same chain
-- WITHOUT this seed. Every changed value traces to metadata/, and none reverts a value the
-- baseline set on purpose:
--   * AllowUserSearchAPI = 0 and AutoUpdateAllowUserSearchAPI = 0 on all 6 entities (#26:
--     secure messaging content stays out of global search)
--   * AllowDeleteAPI = 0 on Portal Sessions, Portal Magic Links, Secure Messages, File Requests
--   * Secure Threads Configuration: left-nav form layout; the 4 relationships off Secure Threads
--     get their UI inclusion (Messages Primary; Message Files and File Requests More; Portal Magic
--     Links None -- auth tokens, not a form surface)
-- Every entity and relationship ID updated here is pinned by the baseline's captured CodeGen.
-- Entity descriptions are NOT set here: they come from the baseline's MS_Description properties.
--
-- -- TRANSFORMS APPLIED TO THE GENERATOR'S OUTPUT ---------------------------------------------
--   `EXEC [${flyway:defaultSchema}]` -> `EXEC [${mjSchema}]`   (36: every proc called is core MJ)
--   Every spCreate (25) is guarded on ID OR the table's natural key, because a host that ran
--   `mj sync push` already holds these rows: ActionCategory by top-level Name, Action by Name,
--   ActionParam by (ActionID, Name), Application by Name. Action.CategoryID and
--   ActionParam.ActionID are re-resolved on the host by name, preferring the pinned ID when the
--   host has it. Nothing else in the generator's output is rewritten. Idempotent: re-running it
--   is a no-op.
--
-- NOT INCLUDED -- metadata-channel-optional/ (Channel Types, Communication Providers). Those
-- target the Channel Messages system, which a standalone MJ + bizapps-common host does not have;
